        "original_id": "e27bdbb0-f56d-5128-82c5-54675769508d",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Works: \"'S Wonderful\", \"Funny Face\"\n- People: Adele Astaire, Allen Kearns, Adele Marie Austerlitz, Lady Charles Cavendish\n- Topics: Broadway musicals, stage performance\n\nFacts:\n- In 1927, the song \"'S Wonderful\" was introduced in the Broadway musical \"Funny Face\" by Adele Astaire and Allen Kearns.\n- Adele Astaire was born as Adele Marie Austerlitz on September 10, 1896.\n- Adele Astaire was also known as Adele, Lady Charles Cavendish.\n- Adele Astaire was an American dancer, stage actress, and singer.\n- Adele Astaire died on January 25, 1981.",
